==English==
{{was wotd|2008|September|29}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|*parlaunce}}, from {{der|en|xno|parlance}}, {{m|fro|parlaunce}}, from {{m|fro|parler|t=to talk}} + {{m|fro|-ance}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɑː.ləns/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɑɹ.ləns/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-parlance.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-parlance.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A certain way of [[speak]]ing, of using words; especially that associated with a particular [[job]] or [[interest]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1836|author=w:James Fenimore Cooper|title="[[s:Eclipse|Eclipse]]"|passage=To my childish fancy, it had seemed an imaginary flag-staff, or, in rustic '''parlance''', the "liberty pole" of some former generation {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1845|author=w:Charles Miner|title=History of Wyoming|section=Letter IX|passage=We approach the contest, still known in the common '''parlance''' of the country, as "the [[w:Pennamite-Yankee War|first Pennimite War]]."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1909|author=w:William Elliot Griffis|title=The Story of New Netherland|section=[[s:The_Story_of_New_Netherland/Chapter_22|Chapter 22]]|passage=The tourist's impression of the country to-day is that of a transported Holland, in which the official language is Dutch and the '''parlance''' of the people is "taki-taki."}}
#* {{RQ:Nabokov Lolita|chapter=12|page=200|passage=At first she "ran a temperature" in American '''parlance''', and I could not resist the exquisite caloricity of unexpected delights—Venus febriculosa—though it was a very languid Lolita that moaned and coughed and shivered in my embrace.}}
# Of a word, the quality of being [[lexicalize]]d; especially as [[jargon]] or [[slang]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Stanley Oluka|title=Performance Management System and Employee Performance in Amuria Health Centre IV, Eastern Uganda|text=Its use at a variety of levels, including the individual and organisational level, make it a varied term that has '''parlance''' in organisational development, performance management and talent management.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|rare}} Speech, [[discussion]] or [[debate]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1849|author=w:Lady Charlotte Guest|title=''[[w:The Mabinogion|The Mabinogion]]''|section="[[s:The_Mabinogion/Peredur_the_Son_of_Evrawc|Peredur the Son of Evrawc]]"|passage=And without further '''parlance''' they fought, {{...}}}}

